{#
   A 404 here has two jobs, not one. The ordinary one is a mistyped or moved URL.
   The other is by design: **a switched-off feature 404s** — that is how the
   gating model makes a feature not exist rather than merely hiding its menu
   entry. So the wording is "this is not part of this site" rather than "something
   went wrong"; the second sends people hunting a bug that isn't there.

   It stops at that deliberately. *Which* feature is off is written to the missing
   page log for the admin, not onto a page anyone can probe.
#}
{% include '@Twig/Exception/_error_page.html.twig' with {
    error_code: 404,
    error_title: 'error.not_found.title'|trans,
    error_message: 'error.not_found.message'|trans,
    error_hint: 'error.not_found.hint'|trans,
    error_variant: 'error.not_found.variant'|trans,
    error_icon: 'missing'
} only %}
